<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body { font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, Helvetica, Arial; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">2013 Lion Honor Roll-NCAA (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000;">
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_1 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_2 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_3 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_4 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_5 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_1_col_6 }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for row in data_rows_1 %}
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_1 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_2 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_3 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_4 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_5 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_6 }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">2013 Scholar Athletes</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000;">
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_1 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_2 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_3 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_4 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_5 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_2_col_6 }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for row in data_rows_2 %}
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_1 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_2 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_3 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_4 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_5 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_6 }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Presidential Academic Excellence Award-NCAA (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The Presidential Academic Excellence Award athlete is a student who has earned a cumulative grade point average of 4.00, has attended {{ attendance_count }} for at least two terms, and is recommended by his/her coach.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Lion Honor Roll Student Life Sports (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The Lion Honor Roll recognizes student athletes who have earned a 3.0+ for a given term and are recommended by their coaches.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Scholar Athlete-Student Life Sports (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The Lionwood Athletes Scholar athlete is a student who has earned a cumulative grade point average of 3.0 or higher, and have been recommended by his/her coach.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">2013 Lion Honor Roll Student Life Sports (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <table style="width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse;">
      <thead>
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #000;">
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_1 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_2 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_3 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_4 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_5 }}</th>
          <th style="text-align: left; padding: 5px;">{{ header_row_3_col_6 }}</th>
        </tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        {% for row in data_rows_3 %}
        <tr style="border-bottom: 1px solid #eee;">
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_1 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_2 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_3 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_4 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_5 }}</td>
          <td style="padding: 5px;">{{ row.col_6 }}</td>
        </tr>
        {% endfor %}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">2013 Lionwood University Honors College (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">Honors scholars are students who are enrolled in the Honors College and have completed at least one course for Honors credit in pursuit of University Honors at graduation.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Phi Alpha Theta (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">Phi Alpha Theta is the National Honors Society for history majors. Nominees must complete at least 12 hours of history with a 3.1 GPA or above. They must also maintain a 3.0 cumulative GPA.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Pi Delta Phi (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The Lionwood chapter (Zeta Pi) of the national French honor society recognizes students who have shown superior achievement in the study of the French language and its literatures. Members must have 3.0 GPA in French, 3.0 GPA overall, and AND rank in the top 35% of their class.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Pi Gamma Mu (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The international honor society Pi Gamma Mu fosters excellence in the social sciences and promotes cooperation among them. Membership is extended to juniors, seniors, graduate students, and faculty members. Students must have a cumulative grade point average of 3.5 or higher overall in the social sciences and must have completed at least 20 credit hours in the social sciences.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Pi Mu Epsilon (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">This society recognizes students who have completed two semesters of calculus and two semesters of math above calculus with a 3.3 GPA, with a cumulative GPA of 3.2 or higher, and have been recommended by the mathematics faculty.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Pi Sigma Alpha (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The national honor society Pi Sigma Alpha stimulates "scholarship and intelligent interest in political science." The Lionwood chapter was founded in 1999 and is extended to juniors, seniors, graduate students, and faculty members. Students must have a cumulative grade point average of 3.5 in political science, a 3.0 overall average, and completed at least 10 hours of political science coursework.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Sigma Delta Pi (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">The Lionwood chapter (iota Xi) of the national collegiate Spanish honor society recognizes students ranking in the upper 35 percent of their class (sophomore, junior, or senior) who have shown superior achievement in courses in Hispanic language, culture, and literature.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Sigma Tau Delta (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
    <p style="text-align: center; font-size: 10pt;">Sigma Tau Delta is the International English Honors Society. Sigma Tau Delta's central purpose is to recognize students of the English language and literature. The organization was re-founded at Lionwood University in 2013.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <h1 style="text-align: center; font-size: 20pt; margin-bottom: 5px;">Who's Who Among Students in American Universities and Colleges (Continued)</h1>
  <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
